fmgen: the self feedback without shifting a negative number

Operator::CalcFB() and CalcFBL() scale the self feedback up before shifting it
down by the feedback amount. The value is signed, and the left shift of a
negative number is undefined behaviour, which UndefinedBehaviorSanitizer stops
the program at:

  src/chips/np2/fmgen_fmgen.cpp:839:16: runtime error: left shift of negative
  value -39

Here a multiplication would not do: the scale is 2^17, which the sum of two
operator outputs can carry past the end of an int, and a signed overflow is
undefined as well. Shifting in an unsigned type and converting back gives the
bits the code already worked with, and every step of it is defined.

This is ADLplug-Next's own patch, applied to the submodule by
cmake/Patches.cmake when CMake configures, and it goes away once the change is
upstream.

diff --git a/src/chips/np2/fmgen_fmgen.cpp b/src/chips/np2/fmgen_fmgen.cpp
index d5b30d3..c91f6ff 100644
--- a/src/chips/np2/fmgen_fmgen.cpp
+++ b/src/chips/np2/fmgen_fmgen.cpp
@@ -836,7 +836,7 @@ inline FM::ISample FM::Operator::CalcFB(uint fb)
 	int pgin = PGCalc() >> (20+FM_PGBITS-FM_OPSINBITS);
 	if (fb < 31)
 	{
-		pgin += ((in << (1 + IS2EC_SHIFT)) >> fb) >> (20+FM_PGBITS-FM_OPSINBITS);
+		pgin += ((ISample)((uint32)in << (1 + IS2EC_SHIFT)) >> fb) >> (20+FM_PGBITS-FM_OPSINBITS);
 	}
 	out_ = LogToLin(eg_out_ + SINE(pgin));
 	dbgopout_ = out2_;
@@ -854,7 +854,7 @@ inline FM::ISample FM::Operator::CalcFBL(uint fb)
 	int pgin = PGCalcL() >> (20+FM_PGBITS-FM_OPSINBITS);
 	if (fb < 31)
 	{
-		pgin += ((in << (1 + IS2EC_SHIFT)) >> fb) >> (20+FM_PGBITS-FM_OPSINBITS);
+		pgin += ((ISample)((uint32)in << (1 + IS2EC_SHIFT)) >> fb) >> (20+FM_PGBITS-FM_OPSINBITS);
 	}
 
 	out_ = LogToLin(eg_out_ + SINE(pgin) + ams_[chip_->GetAML()]);
